Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/openconfig/goyang v1.6.4-0.20251113201521-a80f2799d7b9

goyang gives every copy of an rpc or action the input and output of the
original. Entry.dup copies the RPC field by pointer, so each use of a grouping
that defines an action shares one input and one output, parented to the
grouping. Modules.Process applies augments and deviations to that shared
entry, so one aimed at the parameters of one use reaches every use, against
RFC 7950 Section 7.17: "This node is called the augment's target node. ...
It is augmented with the nodes defined in the substatements that follow the
"augment" statement." The target is the one use's input, not every use's.
Entry.dup now copies the input and output with dup() and parents them to the
copy.

An input or output goyang creates for an augment, when the action declares
the other one only, had no parent, so a path climbing from a leaf in it
reached nothing; RFC 7950 Section 6.4.1: "The node representing the operation
being defined has the operation's input parameters as children." Find now
parents it to its operation.

Proposed upstream as https://github.com/openconfig/goyang/pull/318.
Delete this patch once the goyang release go.mod requires contains the fix.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a vendored
module".

